From cb8e38a74343ab5515274e0d6186e876054b1384 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 03:47:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-53: AutoSize for labels, as in BCB6's Object
 Inspector (0.53.0)

A generated AutoSize label is written "width:136px; ... width:auto" -- the
size follows its text. Until now such a label could not be resized at all
(the handles failed with "not a px value in its own style"), with no way to
say "stop following the text".
- properties panel: an AutoSize checkbox for labels. Off = its width and
  height become the size it has now (px, the auto declarations and the old
  px duplicates go -- htmledit.setStyle keeps the last one); on = auto again.
  Disabled when the label is locked; several selected: only the labels.
- a resize handle (or Width / Height typed in the panel) on an AutoSize
  label now says why: turn AutoSize off first (BCB6 behaves the same).
- DFM: a TLabel's AutoSize is True unless its .dfm says False (VCL's
  "default True"); the difference list compares it (IoSetView: 26 labels
  drawn at a fixed size, AutoSize in the DFM -- one pattern line).

Tests: lib (the TLabel default, "False", a button none; a fixed-size label
differs from the DFM), probe (Label1 / Label82: the handle refused with the
reason, off writes the measured size, on writes auto), real VS Code (Label1
on in the page and the DFM; off -> its measured px in the source, the autos
gone; ONE undo).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
